('h2', "1.5  Unprofessional Conduct / Professional Misconduct"),
('p', "Professional misconduct (also called **infamous conduct in a professional respect**) means any act or omission by a registered practitioner which is regarded as disgraceful or dishonourable by his professional colleagues of good repute and competence. In India, misconduct by doctors is governed by Chapter 7 of the **Indian Medical Council (Professional Conduct, Etiquette and Ethics) Regulations, 2002**; the same principles are applied by analogy to paramedical staff through institutional and Clinical Establishments Act rules."),
('n', [
    "**Falsification of reports** \u2014 fabricating, altering, back-dating or issuing a report without performing the test.",
    "**Breach of confidentiality** \u2014 disclosing results to unauthorised persons, discussing patients on social media.",
    "**Working beyond one's competence** or performing procedures for which one is not authorised.",
    "**Negligence** \u2014 wrong labelling, sample mix-up, failing to inform a critical value.",
    "**Reporting for duty under the influence** of alcohol or drugs.",
    "**Accepting or giving 'cuts', commissions, kickbacks** for referring samples to a particular laboratory \u2014 explicitly prohibited (a form of **fee-splitting** or **dichotomy**).",
    "**Advertising and canvassing** for patients in an undignified manner; making exaggerated claims.",
    "**Sex determination of a foetus** and disclosure of foetal sex \u2014 a criminal offence under the **PC-PNDT Act, 1994**.",
    "**Issuing false certificates** (fitness, sickness, medico-legal).",
    "**Refusal to treat / discrimination**, especially against HIV-positive patients.",
    "**Sexual misconduct or harassment** of patients or colleagues.",
    "**Violation of biosafety and waste-disposal rules** endangering the public.",
    "**Rudeness, abusive behaviour or physical violence** at the workplace.",
    "**Covering up** \u2014 shielding an unqualified person or concealing another's serious error."
]),
('warn', ["**Malpractice vs Misconduct vs Negligence** \u2014 examiners love this distinction:",
          "- **Negligence** = failure to exercise reasonable care \u2192 leads to a *civil suit for damages*.",
          "- **Malpractice** = negligence or improper conduct *by a professional* in the course of professional duty \u2192 civil and sometimes criminal liability.",
          "- **Professional misconduct** = conduct disgraceful to the profession (may not harm any individual patient, e.g. advertising) \u2192 leads to *disciplinary action by the council*, i.e. warning, suspension or **erasure of name from the register**."]),

